[signal arg="dialogue_ended"]
join mc left
join boyfriend right
boyfriend: How was your day, little love?
mc: Nothing much, it's all a bit of a blur...
mc: Just the same as always, I think.
mc (Sad): Staring at a screen for hours gives me a bit of a headache...
mc (Neutral): ...
mc: H-How was... yours?
He tilts his head to the side, intrigued by my question.
boyfriend (Ominous): My day?
boyfriend (Neutral): Oh my...
boyfriend: I... worked. At my... job.
mc (Neutral): ... I know you did... but how was it?
boyfriend (Happy): Hm? that is all.
boyfriend (Blushing): I did miss you. Terribly.
boyfriend (Neutral): On the way home, all I could think of was what I would cook today for you...
mc (Sad): I see...
I didn't know why, but he would always avoid the subject when it came to me asking questions about him
At the same time I felt welcomed into his warm presence, there was always this barrier blocking me from him.
Whatever it is that he is afraid of telling me... I want to someday let him realize I want to listen.